Adds a flashlight to Far Cry 2. Press [b]L[/b] to turn it on or off.

[size=4][b]What it adds[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]A real light[/b], the same kind the cars' headlights use, that follows where you look.[/*]
[*][b]Its own key[/b], L by default. Change it in Options → Controls like any other key.[/*]
[*][b]Guards can see it.[/b] At night a guard looking your way spots the light, and one you shine it on notices you even with their back turned.[/*]
[*][b]A click[/b] when you switch it, and a [b]HUD icon[/b] above the diamond counter that shows whether it's on.[/*]
[/list]

In [b]Options → Mod Configuration Menu[/b] you can pick a small, medium or large beam, and turn its shadows off.

[size=4][b]How to install (Vortex)[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/about/vortex/]Vortex[/url] and its Far Cry 2 extension.[/*]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] on this page and enable the mod. Vortex also offers to get [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], which this mod needs.[/*]
[*]Start the game with the [b]Play[/b] button in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
Not using Vortex? Install it with JackAll instead, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Needs Far Cry 2 patch 1.03[/b], Steam or GOG, and FCSE 1.4.0 or later.[/*]
[*][b]Works with other mods that add keys.[/b][/*]
[*][b]Mods that replace the HUD[/b] can hide the icon if they load last. The flashlight still works.[/*]
[/list]
